# Wave W17-Q (Route 122): pyre sand — grave-shore sand: an ash-pale, grey-quiet sand on Mt. Requiem’s island shore, fine ash flecks standing in it like something remembered (design: the Pyre water — boats keep a respectful circle; the island keeps everything else). Route 122’s own sand — greyer and quieter than Route 105’s stone-pale tomb sand and far from Route 109’s bright gold: this shore is kept at a mourner’s register.
